{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 1, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a nobleman and a prominent figure in the Kingdom of Jerusalem during the 12th century. He was born around 1140 and was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. *Early Life and Family* Raymond III was a member of the House of Toulouse and was related to several powerful nobles in the Kingdom of Jerusalem. His mother Hodierna was the sister of Queen Melisende of Jerusalem and his father Raymond II was the ruler of the County of Tripoli.\n\nAfter his father's death in 1152 Raymond III became the Count of Tripoli at a young age and was placed under the regency of his mother Hodierna. *Reign and Military Campaigns* Raymond III took part in several military campaigns during his reign including the Battle of Hattin in 1187 where he played a crucial role. He was one of the few leaders who managed to escape the battle and flee to Tyre. Raymond III was a skilled military leader and was known for his bravery and strategic thinking.\n\nRaymond III was also involved in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem and played a key role in the succession crisis that followed the death of King Amalric I in 1174. *Succession Crisis and Later Life* He supported the claim of Baldwin IV to the throne and was a member of the regency council that governed the kingdom during Baldwin's minority. Raymond III died in 1187 without an heir and the County of Tripoli was inherited by his godson Raymond IV who was the son of Bohemond III of Antioch.\n\nThroughout his life Raymond III was known for his loyalty to the Kingdom of Jerusalem and his commitment to the defense of the Christian states in the Holy Land. He was a respected leader and a skilled military commander who played a significant role in the history of the Crusades. Raymond III's legacy continued to be felt long after his death and his memory was remembered by the nobles and chroniclers of the time.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.018178174272179604}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": " III", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0005535738891921937}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0012475810945034027}, {"token": " nob", "logprob": -0.1571742594242096}, {"token": "leman", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.025386089459061623}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.6957604289054871}, {"token": " prominent", "logprob": -1.7926561832427979}, {"token": " figure", "logprob": -0.20177768170833588}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -5.125986263010418e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " Kingdom", "logprob": -0.22878225147724152}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Jerusalem", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " during", "logprob": -2.7656173188006505e-05}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": "12", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "th", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " century", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -3.349725011503324e-05}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.00020966715237591416}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -2.682172998902388e-05}, {"token": " born", "logprob": -0.2024192214012146}, {"token": " around", "logprob": -0.2014271765947342}, {"token": " ", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "114", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.0015026956098154187}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.6967816948890686}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -2.0265558760002023e-06}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -0.0004899493651464581}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Raymond", "logprob": -6.305972783593461e-05}, {"token": " II", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count